Hi Alec,

Can you clarify the observation processes a bit?
Are you measuring counts at sites, or measuring as a point process (like in line transect data)?

I’ll try to have a look at the .zip file. Normally, if you can build two observation models separately in inlabru,
it should in principle just require feeding it both those likelihoods and joining the list of model components into one, but the details of the common model components might depend on the precision model structure.

Finn

